"" {TEXT 217 11 " Problem 1." }{TEXT 324 3 "   " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 324 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 324 44 "Generate 8 random 3 by \+
3 matrices using the " }{TEXT 218 12 "RandomMatrix" }{TEXT 324 19 " co
mmand from the  " }{TEXT 219 13 "LinearAlgebra" }{TEXT 324 42 " packag
e. As each matrix is generated use " }{TEXT 220 11 "Eigenvalues" }
{TEXT 324 160 " to compute its eigenvalues. Then take the product of t
he eigenvalues, and check that for each matrix, this product is equal \+
to the determinant of the matrix.  " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 324 0 "" 
}}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 324 1 "[" }{TEXT 221 6 "Hint: " }{TEXT 324 79 
"The product will be complicated algebraically and you will need to ap
ply first " }{TEXT 222 6 "expand" }{TEXT 324 7 ", then " }{TEXT 223 8 
"simplify" }{TEXT 324 132 " to reduce the product of the eigenvalues t
o an integer. First try to do for a single matrix , then make a loop t
o do it 8 times.]  " }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 8 "resta
rt:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 20 "with(LinearAlgebra):
" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 22 "A:=RandomMatrix(3,3);\n
" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 38 "EvA:=simplify(evalf(Eigenvalues(A)));\n" }{MPLTEXT
 1 0 22 "B:=RandomMatrix(3,3);\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 37 "EvB:=simplify(eval
f(Eigenvalues(B)));" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 1 "\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 3 "C:=" }
{MPLTEXT 1 0 19 "RandomMatrix(3,3);\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 37 "EvC:=simplify
(evalf(Eigenvalues(C)));" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 1 "\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 3 "E:=" }
